  "version": 1,
  "name": "Lean-out 4-day",
  "weeks": 12,
  "progression": "Double progression. Start at a weight that hits the bottom of the rep range at the week's target RIR. Add reps at the same weight each session. When every working set reaches the top of the range at target RIR, add weight next session: +5 lb Smith bench and upper-body machines/cables, +10 lb Smith squat, RDL, hip thrust and leg press, next dumbbell (+5 lb) for dumbbell lifts; reset reps to the bottom of the range. If reps fall below the bottom of the range two sessions in a row, reduce load 5-10% and rebuild. Holding loads steady in a deficit is a win. 'rir' on each exercise is the baseline; use weekPlan for the week's actual RIR (compound=true uses rirCompound, else rirIsolation).",
  "deload": "Weeks 6 and 12: half the working sets (round up), load about 90% of week 5/11, RIR 4 on compounds and 3 on isolation. Week 12 check-in: Mon/Tue do one set of Smith bench and Smith squat at the week-1 start weight to 1 RIR and log reps to compare.",
